text	I did not take **#91 README: the install command says npm instal** into work, because it is assigned to someone else.  **What it asks:** The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  **Why I stopped:** The take-in check printed `#91: assigned to rivera`. You are signed in to GitHub as `kim`, so the issue belongs to rivera. I did not create a branch or worktree, did not assign the issue, did not add a label and did not edit any file.  To go on, tell me one of these: - rivera agrees to hand it over. I then assign the issue to you and do the fix: a one-word change in the README, then a pull request. - You leave it with rivera. Nothing else is needed from me.
person	It is mine now, take it
