text	I took **#91 README: the install command says npm instal** and fixed it, but I could not open the pull request. `gh pr create` failed twice.  **What is done** - **Issue:** I assigned #91 to you and added the label `in progress`, which I first had to create in the repository. rivera is still assigned too, because the command only adds you. If rivera should come off, run `gh issue edit 91 --remove-assignee rivera`. - **Tracker:** I found no duplicates, and no open bug or debt issue on the same code. No other issue came along with this one. - **Fix:** I made the work in a new worktree on the branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`. The change is one line in `README.md:3`: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`. It is in commit `5ab83d6`, and the branch is pushed to `origin`. - **Review:** The change is documents only, so it got one review round. The reviewer found no defect. The rules skip the security review for documents only. - **Check:** The repository has no check command: no `package.json`, no Makefile and no CI. So I ran no check. - **Docs:** I changed `README.md`, the document the issue is about. No other document describes the install command.  **What failed** I ran `gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README"` once with `--body-file` and once with `--body`. Each time `gh` stopped with the error `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. GitHub did not give the reason. The `gh` on this machine seems to be a stand-in that cannot create pull requests. I stopped there and did not try another way, so: - There is no pull request. - I did not ask whether to merge. - #91 is still open.  **Next step:** Open the pull request by hand from the branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`. The description, with `Closes #91` and the `## Review` summary, is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`. When the pull request exists, I can do the merge and the rest of the finishing steps.
